\chapter{Architecture Overview}
\section{System Architecture}

The ClimateProcessingEngine follows a modular, pipeline-based architecture with clear separation of concerns. Figure~\ref{fig:architecture} illustrates the overall system design.

\begin{figure}[H]
    \centering
    \begin{tikzpicture}[node distance=1.5cm, auto, every node/.style={rectangle, draw, minimum width=3cm, minimum height=1cm, align=center, font=\small}]
        \node (config) {Configuration Layer\\\texttt{config.yaml + constants.py}};
        \node (io) [below=of config] {I/O Pipeline\\\texttt{read\_month\_files.py}};
        \node (numeric) [below=of io] {Numerical Engine\\\texttt{distributions.py}};
        \node (result) [below=of numeric] {Result Pipeline\\\texttt{write\_block.py}};
        \node (monitor) [below=of result] {Monitoring\\\texttt{benchmark.py}};
        \draw[->] (config) -- (io);
        \draw[->] (io) -- (numeric);
        \draw[->] (numeric) -- (result);
        \draw[->] (result) -- (monitor);
    \end{tikzpicture}
    \caption{System Architecture Overview}
    \label{fig:architecture}
\end{figure}

\section{Core Components}

\subsection{Configuration Layer (\texttt{constants.py + config.yaml})}
Centralizes all settings in a single YAML file, parsed by \texttt{constants.py}. This ensures consistent configuration across all modules.

\subsection{I/O Pipeline (\texttt{io\_pipeline/*.py})}
Responsible for reading input data from Zarr archives, assembling blocks, and validating loaded data.

\subsection{Numerical Engine (\texttt{numerical\_engine/*.py})}
Performs the core statistical analysis, including window extraction, distribution fitting, and result aggregation.

\subsection{Result Pipeline (\texttt{result\_pipeline/*.py})}
Validates and writes results to the output Zarr store.

\subsection{Monitoring (\texttt{monitoring/*.py})}
Handles logging, checkpointing, and benchmarking.

\subsection{Orchestrator (\texttt{orchestrator/*.py})}
Coordinates the execution flow, managing the block processing loop.

\section{Data Flow}
The data flow follows a linear pipeline:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Load Phase}: Read raw data from input Zarr files for a block of stations
    \item \textbf{Assembly Phase}: Arrange data into a 4D array (station, year, day, variable)
    \item \textbf{Validation Phase}: Validate the assembled data against the data contract
    \item \textbf{Analysis Phase}: For each station, extract windows and fit distributions
    \item \textbf{Result Validation}: Validate analysis results before writing
    \item \textbf{Write Phase}: Write validated results to the output Zarr store
    \item \textbf{Checkpoint}: Record progress for recovery
\end{enumerate}

