\chapter{Data Contract}
\section{Dynamic Distribution Architecture}
Starting from version 2.1, the engine supports a \textbf{dynamic distribution architecture} that allows adding new distributions without reprocessing the raw data.

\subsection{Key Concepts}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Window Cache}: During the initial processing, the engine stores window values (5-day windows for each station and day) in a separate Zarr store (\texttt{window\_cache.zarr}).
    \item \textbf{Modular Distributions}: Each distribution is defined as a dictionary in \texttt{zarr\_schema.py} with its parameters, code, and fitting function.
    \item \textbf{Add Distribution Script}: The \texttt{add\_distribution.py} script reads the window cache, fits a new distribution, and updates the output Zarr with new variables and \texttt{best\_dist}.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Adding a New Distribution}
To add a new distribution (e.g., Logistic):
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Add the distribution to \texttt{DISTRIBUTIONS} in \texttt{zarr\_schema.py}
    \item Implement the fitting function in \texttt{distributions.py} and add it to \texttt{FIT\_FUNCS}
    \item Run \texttt{python add\_distribution.py --dist logistic}
\end{enumerate}
This process does \textbf{not require reading the raw input files again}.

\subsection{Benefits}
\begin{itemize}
    \item No need to reprocess all data for each new distribution
    \item Saves significant time and computational resources
    \item Enables experimentation with different distribution families
    \item Maintains backward compatibility with existing outputs
\end{itemize}


\section{Load Phase Contract}
\subsection{Input}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \texttt{block\_start}: integer – Starting station index
    \item \texttt{block\_size}: integer – Number of stations
    \item \texttt{file\_map}: dict – \texttt{(year, month) → file\_path}
    \item \texttt{year\_list}: list – All years in analysis period
    \item \texttt{doy\_table}: ndarray – Shape \texttt{(N\_YEARS, 13, 32)}
\end{itemize}
\subsection{Output}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \texttt{block\_data}: ndarray – Shape \texttt{(block\_size, N\_YEARS, N\_DAYS, N\_VARS)}
    \item Data type: \texttt{float32}
    \item Memory layout: C-contiguous
    \item Missing values: \texttt{NaN}
\end{itemize}

\section{Window Phase Contract}
\subsection{Input}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \texttt{station\_data}: ndarray – Shape \texttt{(N\_YEARS, N\_DAYS, N\_VARS)}
    \item \texttt{window\_table}: list – 366 entries
\end{itemize}
\subsection{Output}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item List of 366 entries
    \item Each entry: \texttt{ndarray} or \texttt{None}
    \item Non-None arrays contain valid values (NaNs removed)
    \item Length $\ge$ \texttt{MIN\_VALID\_VALUES} = 5
\end{itemize}

\section{Analyze Phase Contract}
\subsection{Input}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \texttt{station\_data}: ndarray – Shape \texttt{(N\_YEARS, N\_DAYS, N\_VARS)}
\end{itemize}
\subsection{Output}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Dict with 87 keys
    \item Each key: ndarray – Shape \texttt{(N\_DAYS,)}
    \item Types: \texttt{int32} for \texttt{best\_dist} and \texttt{count}
    \item Types: \texttt{float32} for all others
\end{itemize}

\section{Write Phase Contract}
\subsection{Input}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \texttt{block\_result}: dict – 87 variables
    \item Each variable: Shape \texttt{(N\_DAYS, block\_size)}
\end{itemize}
\subsection{Output}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Zarr store with 87 variables
    \item Shape: \texttt{(N\_DAYS, n\_stations)}
    \item Coordinated with \texttt{day\_of\_year} and \texttt{point} dimensions
\end{itemize}

