\chapter{Performance Optimization}
\section{Block Size Selection}
The optimal block size depends on available RAM, CPU cache, disk I/O speed, and number of cores. The benchmarking system automatically evaluates block sizes from 500 to 3000 and selects the one with the highest stations-per-second rate.

\section{Parallel Processing}
When \texttt{use\_parallel} is enabled, the engine uses \texttt{multiprocessing} or \texttt{concurrent.futures}; each worker processes a separate block; the \texttt{cores} parameter controls the number of workers.

\section{Memory Management}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Block-based processing}: Data is processed in blocks to limit memory usage
    \item \textbf{Garbage collection}: Active memory is reclaimed after each block
    \item \textbf{NaN handling}: Missing values use \texttt{float32} to reduce memory footprint
    \item \textbf{Chunked Zarr}: Output is stored in chunks for efficient access
\end{enumerate}

\section{Performance Tips}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Use SSD storage for both input and output data
    \item Increase the number of cores if available
    \item Use smaller block sizes if RAM is limited
    \item Disable validation for production runs to reduce overhead
    \item Run on a dedicated machine without memory-intensive applications
\end{enumerate}

% ============================================================
% فصل ۱۱: عیب‌یابی
% ============================================================
\chapter{Troubleshooting}

\section{Common Errors and Solutions}
\subsection{FileNotFoundError}
\begin{lstlisting}[caption=FileNotFoundError]
FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'path/to/file'
\end{lstlisting}
\textbf{Solution:}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Verify the file path in \texttt{config.yaml}
    \item Check that the file exists and is readable
    \item Use absolute paths to avoid ambiguity
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{MemoryError}
\begin{lstlisting}[caption=MemoryError]
MemoryError: Unable to allocate array
\end{lstlisting}
\textbf{Solution:}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Reduce the \texttt{block\_size} in \texttt{config.yaml}
    \item Disable validation for lower memory usage
    \item Use \texttt{use\_parallel: false}
    \item Increase system RAM or use a machine with more memory
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{KeyError}
\begin{lstlisting}[caption=KeyError]
KeyError: 'variable_name'
\end{lstlisting}
\textbf{Solution:}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Check that the variable exists in the input Zarr files
    \item Verify variable naming matches the schema
    \item Ensure the \texttt{VARS} list in \texttt{config.yaml} is correct
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{ImportError}
\begin{lstlisting}[caption=ImportError]
ImportError: No module named 'module_name'
\end{lstlisting}
\textbf{Solution:}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Install missing dependencies
    \item Check Python environment (use \texttt{which python})
    \item Use \texttt{pip install -r requirements.txt}
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{IndentationError}
\begin{lstlisting}[caption=IndentationError]
IndentationError: unexpected indent
\end{lstlisting}
\textbf{Solution:}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Check that Python files use consistent indentation (4 spaces)
    \item Avoid mixing tabs and spaces
    \item Use an editor with Python indentation support
\end{enumerate}

\section{Logging}
The engine logs all major events to:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Console}: Real-time progress information
    \item \textbf{Log file}: \texttt{climatology.log} in the output directory
\end{itemize}
Log levels: \texttt{DEBUG}, \texttt{INFO} (default), \texttt{WARNING}, \texttt{ERROR}.

\section{Debugging Tips}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Set \texttt{logging.level: DEBUG} for more verbose output
    \item Check the log file for detailed error traces
    \item Run a small test with \texttt{block\_size: 100} to verify setup
    \item Use Python's interactive debugger (\texttt{pdb}) for deep troubleshooting
    \item Verify input data quality before large-scale processing
\end{enumerate}

